FriendFlix media server, change 0002 (mediaserver/patches/0002-vaapi-hdr-tonemap-chain.md).
Status: proposed — not applied to the image; needs a source build and hardware confirmation.
A patch to Ferrofin (GPL-3.0-only), so it carries Ferrofin's licence, not the repository's AGPL.
Text before the first "diff --git" line is ignored by git apply and patch.

Subject: [PATCH] hw: skip tonemap_vaapi when the VA driver has no HDR tone mapper

Against v1.5.1. Apply with `git apply` (or `patch -p1`) from the repo root.

On Linux both Intel chains (QSV over VAAPI and VAAPI) tonemap with
`tonemap_vaapi`. intel/media-driver advertises
VAProcFilterHighDynamicRangeToneMapping only on SKUs with FtrHDR. Skylake,
Apollo Lake and the GT1 Kaby/Coffee/Comet Lake parts don't have it. On those
SKUs `tonemap_vaapi` fails while ffmpeg configures its output pad ("VAAPI
driver doesn't support HDR", then "Failed to configure output pad on
Parsed_tonemap_vaapi_N"), so the transcode never starts. Jellyfin has the same
gap. The generated chain is byte-identical to upstream's.

- FfmpegCapabilities: new `vaapi_hdr_tonemap_missing` flag. It defaults to
  false, which keeps upstream behaviour.
- is_intel_vpp_tonemap_available: returns false on Linux when the flag is set.
  The chains then fall through to the OpenCL tonemap, or to no tonemap.
- EncoderValidator: adds VAAPI_HDR_TONEMAP_PROBE_ARGS (a one-frame
  hwupload,tonemap_vaapi graph) and a stderr parser that matches only the
  filter's own refusal.
- VaapiProber: one probe per device for QSV/VAAPI jobs on Linux with VPP
  tonemapping enabled, cached for the process's life. For QSV it opens the
  VAAPI half of the job's own qsv_device_args.
- Tests: the predicate; a QSV chain golden that reproduces the failing chain;
  the fallback chains; the parser; the prober with a stub ffmpeg.

